bin/skilletor-start always prefers the pinned release binary once bin/skilletor-binaries.sha256 exists (k191). There is no switch to run Node or Perl instead -- for a developer checkout that has the pin, for CI that must test a given engine, and for users who want k203 (b) (Node first). Today only `node dist/skilletor.js` or `perl -Ilib script/skilletor` directly does that, which the hooks never call.

Recommendation (from k191, deferred 2026-11-16): SKILLETOR_ENGINE=node or perl makes the starter skip the binary and run that engine (failing loudly when it is missing, except for `hook` calls, which fail open as today); unset or `auto` keeps the current order. Document it in the README's "Which engine runs" and the bundled skill; test it in test/starter.test.ts.

superseded by hub decision 2026-11-25 (no Perl runtime); removal in k275 on branch getty-bun
